  "prompt_text": "Use case: style-transfer. Transform the deer sprite sheet reference into a complete juvenile primitive CATTLE CALF sprite sheet, preserving its ink-and-tone style and exact 2-row by 5-column pose layout. References: first deer sheet = layout/animal style; person and scene = locked style only, do not reproduce background. Exactly TEN separate complete cattle, same individual in all cells. Transparent RGBA landscape, generous transparent margins/gutters, no labels/text/grid/ground/cast shadows. Top row S front three-quarter, 35 degrees toward viewer LEFT from head-on; lower row E right-facing side three-quarter. Camera ~20 degrees down, upper-left light. Calf: warm russet young calf with oversized soft head, short cream-ringed muzzle, large ears, tiny rounded horn buds, short barrel belly, delicately sturdy slightly long legs and small hooves, thin tufted tail, no udder, no accessories. Recognizably juvenile rather than scaled adult. Same stock lineage as russet primitive cattle. Match natural-history pen and restrained two-tone ochre/umber wash. Main contour twice interior ink width. Short hide: only 3 clusters of 2-3 short hatching strokes on shoulder/flank/haunch, all descending upper-left to lower-right. Broad quiet planes; no dense fur. Five columns BOTH rows: STAND four grounded hooves head up; WALK one raised bent foreleg opposite hind step; RUN extended airborne gallop with forelegs forward hindlegs back; GRAZE muzzle at hoof level neck bent low; DEAD completely limp on side horizontally eyes closed legs sideways, no blood. Clear distinct action silhouettes and identical body size across all upright cells. Keep all horns/tails/hooves connected and inside own cell. This is a 96x80 game frame family; anatomy and silhouette must survive reduction. Actual alpha transparency, no colored backdrop.\n",
